        <type>int32_t</type>
        <definition>int32_t pros::c::aivision_reset</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t port)</argsstring>
        <name>aivision_reset</name>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>port</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Resets the AI <ref refid="classpros_1_1v5_1_1Vision" kindref="compound">Vision</ref> sensor to the initial state. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function uses the following values of errno when an error state is reached: ENXIO - The given value is not within the range of V5 ports (1-21). ENODEV - The port cannot be configured as a vision sensor</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>port</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The V5 port number from 1-21</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>PROS_SUCCESS if the operation was successful or PROS_ERR if the operation failed, setting errno.</para>
</simplesect>
<bold>Example</bold> <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">#define<sp/>AIVISION_PORT<sp/>1</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">void<sp/>initialize()<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>aivision_reset(AIVISION_PORT);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
